        <p>A large size Tin, with 'Brush and Holder complete, free per Parcel Post for Is. 4d. in stamps or postal order.</p>
        <p>Copy of unsoli7ited Testimonial, ,selectei out of a number</p>
        <p>received.</p>
        <p>Hawthorne Villa, Linthort.e, Middleshro., Oct. 29, 1892. Mr- M, M. Lawson, Liverpool. DEAR have used some or the " Lawson's Black" on my drawing and dining room fire grates, which my husband brought me to try, with the object of saving the servants the tedious work of black leading, and I think it only right to comply with his desire to inform you that the trial has been most satisfactory in every respect; not only is the saving in time reduced more than three-fourths, and the appearance of the grates muchimproved as compared to blacklead, but the brush and holder you heve introduced en- ables those who use it to do so without in any way blacking or soiling their hands. I may also add that so far the appear- ance has not been affected by the heat of the fires.—Yours respectfully, JENNIE DOVE.</p>
