        <p>VUNCORN UNION.—CONTRACTS for PROVIS- it, lONS anti SUPPLE/3S for the half-year ending September 30th; 1893.</p>
        <p>- The Guardians of the poor of the Runcorn Union are desirous of receiving TENDERS from parties willing to CONTRACT for the supply of New Milk. Futtermilk, Fresh Butter, and Fresh Eggs, (fort welve months), Flour. Oat- meal, Grocedes, Peas, Cheese, salt Butter; Cod Liver and Paraffin Oil; Quinine; Good B2ef. to *onsist of vein and brisket pieces, the price to ineMde about 40 be., per week of the Best Butdaer's Meet for the officers, and sides of Mutton ; Home Cured Bacon; Potatoes ; Wheat Straw; Drapery and Clothing; Men's. Women's. Boy's and Girls' Shoes,of vari, sizes, as per samples to be seen at ..the Workhouse, Dutton, and Shoe Mending; House Coal, (Colliery to be 'lamed). Good Deal Coffins, specifying size and including plate with name, age, and death, to be delivered in the Union when and where required; Coke; Carting at permile, Funerals at per Funeral. _ _ _</p>
        <p>- --- Parties Tendering for the samply of the above-mentioned Goods, will be required to deliver the same at the Workhouse free of cot to the Guard!ana, how and when required. . .</p>
        <p>Tenders toe accompanied with Samples (except Drapery Goods), as far as practicable. The Guardians do not bind themselves to accept the Lowest or any Tender. Persons desirous of Tendering, must app'y by letter, to my office. in Runcorn, for a printed form of Tender, (and none other can be entertained), where a Schedule of the various articles required and further particulars may be obtained. _ _ _</p>
        <p>----- Sealed Tenders addressed to the Guardians, to he for- warded to the Clerk's Office, ,Runeorn, on or before Setwday, the 18th day ot March, 1893, endorsed "Tender for" The Tenders will be opened and considered at a meetinga the Guardians to be held in the Board-room, Dutton, on the 21st day of March, 1893, at two p.m. Parties whose Tenders are accepted must enter into a written Contract, and be prepared te enter into a Bond with two sureties, if required by the Guardians. By Order o; the Board. JOHN' .NSIIT019:.</p>
        <p>Clerk to the Guardians. RUnCOrllt 10th March, 1893.</p>
