        <p>LOT I.—All those THREE FREEHOLD HOUSES, situate and being Nos. 5,7, and 9, in Flag-lane, Warrington, and having a frontage thereto of 91 feet. 6 inches, or thereabouts, and TEN COTTAGES, situate and being Not. 1, 3,5, 7, and 9, in Hughes' Court, and Nos. 2,4, 6,2, and 10, in Cambria- place, and another COTTAGE situate and being No. 19. in Cambria-place, Warrington, with the STABLES and yacent LANDS adjoining thereto, and having a frontage to Golborne- street aforesaid of 43 feet, 6 inches or thereabouts. The site of this lot contains 1889 square yards of land or thereabouts. LOT 2.—A1l that fully-licensed PUBLIC HOUSE called " The Millstone" situate at the Corner of Sankey street, and Golborne-street, Warrington, and being No. 56 Sankey-street and No. 1 Golborne-street aforesaid, having a frontage of 17 feet 10 inches to Sankey-street, and 54 feet 10 inches to Golborne-street, and containing in the whole 152 square yards of land or thereabouts. The tenure is leasehold for the residue of a term of 99 years from the 11th day of May, 1849, subject to an apportioned annual ground rent of £2. LOT 3.—A1l that leasehold SHOP, DWELLINGHOUSE and PREN ISES, situate and being No. 54, Sankey-street, Warrington, in the occupation of Mr. J. Lawton as yearly tenant thereof, having a frontage of 16 feet, 10 inches to Sankey-st. aforesaid, and containing in the wnole 88 square yards of land or thereabouts. This lot is held for the residue of a term of 99 years from the Ilth day of May, 1849. sub- ject than apportioned annual ground rent ef £l. LOT 4. -All that LEASEHOLD DWELLING-HOUSE ad- joining Lot 2, situate on the east side of Golborne-et,, War- -ington, in the occupation of Mr. John Dooley, as yearly! tenant thereof, and having a frontage of 22 feet 11 inches to Golborne-et. aforesaid, and containing in the whole 109 square yards of land or thereabouts. This lot is held for the residue of a term of 99 years from the 11th day of May, 1849.1 subject to an apportioned annual ground rent of £l. LOT 5.—A1l that leasehold PLOT OF LAND adjoining Lot 4, situate on the East side of Golborne-street. Warring- ton • together with the HAMPER MANUFACTORY and STONE ROOM, thereon erected, now in the occupation of Mr. Thomas Hutchinson, as yearly tenant thereof, and hav- ing a frontage of 84 feet 2 inches to Golborne-street afore- said, and containing in the whole 438 square yards of land or thereabouts. This lotus held for the residue of a term of 99 years from the 11th day of May, 1849 subject to an appor- tioned annual ground rent of Rl. LOT 6.—A1l that leasehold PLOT of LAND adjoining Lot 5, situate on the East side of Golborne-st..Warrington, together with the STABLING, WAREHOUSE and STORES erected therein now In the occupation of Mr. William Barlow as yearly tenant thereof, and having a frontage of 4 feet 7 inches to Golborne-et., aforesaid, and containing in the whole 238 square yards of land or thereabouts. This lot is held for the residue of a term of 99 years from the 11th day of May 1849, subject thaw apportioned annual rent of El. LOT 7.—A1l that old established and excellent fully. licensed FREEHOLD INN known as "The Nags Head" situate and bring Nos. 26 and 28 in Sankey-st., Warrington, with the stables, yard. and outbuildings belonging thereto and covering an area of 1,289 square yards or thereabouts, and having a frontage to Sankey-et. of 45 feet 6 inches or thereabouts.</p>
        <p>LOT 8. All that FREEHOLD SHOP, and DWELLING HOUSE, situate and being No. 301 n Sankey-st., Warrington, now in the occupation of Mr. F. J. Dell, and having a front' age of 29 feet 11 inches Cr thereabouts to Sankey-st. afore- said, and containing in the whole 52 square yards of land or thereabouts. This lot will include one room on the ground floor and the cellars under the premises now held with Lot 7.</p>
        <p>LOT 9.—A1l that FREEHOLD SHOP, DWELLING- HOUSE and OUTBUILD INGS, situate and being Nos. 22 and 24, Sankey-street. Warrington, now in the occupation of Mr. T. H. Poole, and held by him for the residue of a term of 10 years.of which six years are unexpired.together with the LARGE ROOM used by the Freemasons. This lot has a frontage to Sankey-street aforeraid, of 48 feet or thereabouts, and contains in the whole 349 scpsare yards of land or there- abouts.</p>
        <p>LOT 10.—All that freehold, FULLY-LICENSED INN, known as " The King's Arms," situate in Lane Head. Low- ton near Newton-le-Willows, with the Club Room, outbuild• fogs, stables, coach-house, loft and Building Land thereto, belonging, containing 3,115 square yards of land or there- abouts.</p>
