        <p>The simplest manner for man to secure immunity from disease is to obsers e and follow these laws as far as practic- able, and if illness overtakes him to take as remedies only such preparations as are supplied by nature. The only NA.T MILL remedies are vegetable, and the most renowned and efficient vegetable remedy of the present age is sawiTym Evans Quinine Bitters.</p>
