        <p>RUNCORN, WESTON AND HALT-ON WATE RWORKS CO. The half yearly meeting of this company was held in the small hall of the Public Haleon Monday afternoon. Mr. J. Brundrit, J.P., chairman of the directors presided, and there were present Messrs. W. Whittaker, J. Simpson, W. Hayes, J. Ashton (solicitor), W. F. Salkeid (sec.),‘ and W. Jones (assistant see.) I The directers' report states that the revenue accouut Shows a balance et £731 175., including £247 4s. 11d., brought from the previous half year out of which the directors recemtnend a dividend to be declared at the 41 per cent, per annum free of income tax. This would absorb £712 10s., leaving a balance of £l9 7s. to be car- ried forwent. In consideration of the great interest at the present taken in the Water Works by the ratepayers, conse- quent upon the proposal to purchase them by the Run- corn Board of Commissioners, the balance sheet of the Company for the past half year, which we append Will be welcomed. The Debtor side of the CAPITAL ACCOUNT is Made up a=t follows :-3,000 shares £lO each,E3o,ooo ; Preference stock, £20,000 ; depreciation fund, £1,000; debenture stock, £2,400 •, total, £53,400. The credit side reads :-Gross expenditure to June 30th, 1892, £53,235 193. 4d. ; extension of main in Hope-st., £2 :is. Bd. ; balance, £l6l 3s. ; total, £53,400. Balance Teal last lielf year, £997 4s. 11d; dividend at 5 per cent, 5O; £247 4s. 11d. Water rents received Sept. 72, £1,212 17s. lid.; fittings received September 30th, -ree_e Os. al. ; £1,281 18s. ld.. Water rents re- elved December 31st, £1,015 6s. 3d. ; fittings received reember 31st, £5O is. 10d.; £1,065 Bs. id. Owing 'ol' water sold by meter December 31st, £217 10s. 3d. ; ring for fittings and meter rents December 31st, £6B 2d. 3 • ' owing for water rates due December 18t, £364 18s. 2d. ; £650 16s. 78. Transfers ~.nt stock fees 2s. 68., and weighing for farmers 6d Credit, ss. ; coals in stock, £lO ; £3,255 12s. 88. Or :-Amount owine for water ren