        <p>MR. DE COBAIN BEFORE THE MAGISTRATES. E. S. W. de Cobain, ex-member of Parliament for East Belfast, was, on Saturday, brought up on remand at Belfast Police Court, charged with immoral offences. It was resolved to hear the case in private, even the re- presentatives of the Press being excluded from court. After the examination of three witnesses, accused was remanded for a week and allowed bail—himself in £5OO and two sureties of £250.</p>
